# Auto-push to GitHub

The site is served by GitHub Pages from `main` on https://github.com/Fastige/Paintballer
(live at https://fastige.github.io/Paintballer/). The user wants every change live without asking.

After finishing and verifying any code change:

1. If `field-mapper.js` / `field-mapper.css` / `main.js` / `styles.css` changed, bump its `?v=` query in the HTML that loads it.
2. Stage only the files you changed (never `git add -A`; unrelated local edits may exist).
3. Commit with a short, descriptive sentence, e.g. `Add playhead to shoot timeline.`
4. `git push origin main`
5. Tell the user it was pushed and that Pages takes ~1 minute to update.

If the push fails (auth, conflicts), report the error instead of forcing it. Never `git push --force`.
